<h1>SpotCheck — Xylem PDF Quality &amp; Visual Inspection Engine</h1>
<p><b>Repository:</b> giriharan007/SpotCheck--Xylem<br><b>Primary language:</b> Python (98.4%)<br><b>Secondary languages:</b> Batchfile (1.3%), Shell (0.3%)</p>

<h2>1. Executive Summary</h2>
<p>SpotCheck is a desktop quality-assurance application for comparing an English technical-manual PDF with one or more translated PDFs. It detects missing or reordered TOC topics, barcode and QR-code problems, missing/extra/moved graphics, image-count mismatches, layout-region defects, text collisions, untranslated English, document metadata differences, and page-level visual differences.</p>
<p>The system has two deliberately separated layers: <code>core/</code> contains headless PDF and image-inspection logic, while <code>gui/</code> contains the Xylem-branded desktop interface. Results are shown interactively and exported to a multi-sheet Excel workbook with comparison and evidence images.</p>

<h2>2. Runtime Architecture</h2>
<pre>run_gui.py
  └── gui.app_window.SpotCheckApp
        ├── core.pipeline.run_quality_inspection()
        ├── gui.region_dialog.RegionInspectorFrame
        ├── gui.comparison_gallery.ComparisonGalleryFrame
        ├── gui.text_checks_tab.TextChecksFrame
        └── gui.metadata_tab.MetadataFrame

core.pipeline
  ├── core.docscan       shared cached page scans / multiprocessing
  ├── core.toc           TOC numerics and topic page mapping
  ├── core.barcode_qr    barcode and QR validation
  ├── core.crop_images   graphic extraction and cropping
  ├── core.compare_crops visual crop matching
  ├── core.image_counts  symmetric graphic counting
  ├── core.region_engine stylesheet-region checks
  ├── core.page_diff     full-page graphic differences
  ├── core.text_overlap  colliding text detection
  ├── core.untranslated  English-left-behind detection
  ├── core.metadata      document facts and column detection
  └── openpyxl           Excel report generation</pre>

<h2>3. Complete Feature Inventory</h2>
<h3>3.1 Input and batch processing</h3>
<ul><li>Accepts a master PDF file or a folder containing exactly one PDF.</li><li>Accepts a translated PDF or a folder of translated PDFs.</li><li>Validates paths and rejects ambiguous master folders.</li><li>Creates output folders automatically.</li><li>Remembers valid paths and the selected template between sessions.</li><li>Runs long inspections on background threads and reports named progress stages.</li></ul>

<h3>3.2 TOC and translation structure</h3>
<ul><li>Reads PDF bookmarks/outlines with PyMuPDF.</li><li>Compares numeric topic identifiers such as <code>1</code>, <code>1.1</code>, and <code>3.2.1</code>, independent of translated titles.</li><li>Detects missing, extra, and reordered topics.</li><li>Builds topic page spans and maps master pages to translated pages after reflow.</li><li>Falls back to page-number matching when no usable outline exists.</li></ul>

<h3>3.3 Barcode and QR-code checks</h3>
<ul><li>Uses Pyzbar/ZBar decoding, OpenCV QR/barcode fallback detectors, and decode-independent structural detection.</li><li>Records code type, decoded data where available, bounding box, page number, and detection method.</li><li>Compares master and translation counts and page locations.</li><li>Excludes barcodes and QR codes from ordinary visual image comparison because their data legitimately changes by language/document.</li><li>Reports <code>CHECK (No Detector)</code> instead of falsely passing a 0/0 result when no detector is available.</li></ul>

<h3>3.4 Graphic extraction and comparison</h3>
<ul><li>Extracts raster images, vector diagrams, logos, icons, hazard symbols, and pictures inside tables.</li><li>Renders pages, masks text, clusters connected ink regions, and removes page furniture.</li><li>Recognizes ruled table lattices and removes text-only table grids.</li><li>Excludes blank regions, barcodes, QR codes, margins, thumb tabs, separators, and isolated rules.</li><li>Groups crops by TOC topic when possible and by page otherwise.</li><li>Uses safe Windows-compatible topic names, reserved-name handling, path-length protection, and page-folder fallback.</li><li>Searches each master crop across translated pages with OpenCV normalized template matching.</li><li>Uses coarse-to-fine matching, credibility thresholds, topic-scoped searches, page mapping, tie-breaking by proximity, and repeated-crop caching.</li><li>Creates side-by-side comparison PNGs with similarity, expected page, translated page, and status.</li></ul>

<h3>3.5 Symmetric image counts</h3>
<ul><li>Counts graphics in both documents instead of only searching for master graphics.</li><li>Catches graphics added to translations and graphics deleted from translations.</li><li>Compares per topic when both documents have TOCs, otherwise compares document totals.</li><li>Uses the same graphic detector and margins as crop extraction so the two checks agree.</li></ul>

<h3>3.6 Stylesheet Region Inspector</h3>
<ul><li>Draws, moves, resizes, deletes, and previews regions on rendered master pages.</li><li>Supports nested regions such as Region 1.1 and automatic renumbering.</li><li>Supports first-page, last-page, all-page, odd-page, and even-page scopes.</li><li>Supports mirrored-layout alternative groups where any variant may pass.</li><li>Supports exact text, visual-only, presence-only, same-pattern, scope-only, and normal layout/presence modes.</li><li>Supports editable expected text, pinned text, token-snapped scoped exact matching, barcode/QR presence checks, per-region tolerances, and per-region thresholds.</li><li>Uses TOC page mapping, edge-based sheet-size anchoring, per-sheet geometry, and optional scale-with-page behavior.</li></ul>

<h3>3.7 Text quality checks</h3>
<ul><li><b>Text overlap:</b> finds text spans whose actual ink collides, avoiding false positives caused only by font bounding boxes.</li><li><b>Not translated:</b> compares normalized translated lines against an English master inventory and uses English function-word density as supporting evidence.</li><li>Skips first and last pages by default because covers and back matter may intentionally remain English.</li><li>Produces evidence images and publishes findings to both the Text Checks and Review tabs.</li></ul>

<h3>3.8 Metadata and layout inspection</h3>
<ul><li>Reports file size, pages, sheet size, orientation, dimensions, rotation, encryption, PDF version, producer, title, and TOC-entry count.</li><li>Classifies ISO A0–A8, Letter, Legal, Tabloid, and custom page dimensions.</li><li>Detects text columns using body-line projections and gutter analysis.</li><li>Optionally excludes tables to prevent table gaps from being mistaken for document columns.</li><li>Samples evenly distributed pages and can list every page.</li><li>Highlights translated documents that differ from the master in page count, sheet size, or columns.</li></ul>

<h3>3.9 Review and page-diff workflow</h3>
<ul><li>Displays region, crop, overlap, and untranslated findings in one gallery.</li><li>Filters all, passed, and needs-review results.</li><li>Uses a scalable Treeview/list-plus-preview design instead of thousands of widgets.</li><li>Provides keyboard navigation and external image opening.</li><li>Opens a synchronized side-by-side whole-page diff.</li><li>Classifies full-page graphics as missing, extra, or moved while masking translated prose.</li><li>Safely deletes only comparison PNGs inside the application’s comparison-output tree.</li></ul>

<h3>3.10 Reporting</h3>
<p><code>core.pipeline</code> creates <code>PDF_Quality_Inspection_Report.xlsx</code> with:</p>
<ol><li>Overview</li><li>TOC</li><li>Barcode &amp; QR</li><li>Images</li><li>Image Counts</li><li>Meta Data</li><li>Stylesheet Result</li><li>Text Overlap</li><li>Not Translated</li></ol>
<p>The workbook contains styled headers, borders, automatic column sizing, colored pass/fail cells, page movement, similarity, evidence details, active margins, region results, metadata, and defect counts.</p>

